01:14:52.150 --> 01:15:00.000
month. The virus has been found in cervical secretions, but in very, very small amounts.

01:15:00.000 --> 01:15:03.970
from cervical secretions per se is rather remote.

01:15:03.970 --> 01:15:05.240
At any rate...

01:15:05.240 --> 01:15:07.240
So it sounds, from the way you describe it,

01:15:07.240 --> 01:15:12.840
that this disease can be quite readily transmitted to women.

01:15:12.840 --> 01:15:15.020
Yes, very readily transmitted to women.

01:15:15.020 --> 01:15:19.610
But then perhaps more difficult for women to transmit it back to men.

01:15:19.610 --> 01:15:21.440
That's what we suspect epidemiologically,

01:15:21.440 --> 01:15:25.970
at least in the United States and in the Western Europe.

01:15:25.970 --> 01:15:28.870
Now, is the disease transmitted by oral sex?

01:15:30.000 --> 01:15:35.320
don't know. There's really no evidence one way or another. It's hard to find a group

01:15:35.320 --> 01:15:41.520
of individuals who participate only in oral sex and have no other kind of sexual exposure.

01:15:41.520 --> 01:15:45.580
One can do it by some sorts of statistical analysis, but it would be hard to prove that

01:15:45.580 --> 01:15:50.940
a specific case of oral sex definitively transmitted the AIDS virus.

01:15:50.940 --> 01:15:59.670
Dr. Krim, is kissing a risk?

01:16:00.000 --> 01:16:06.010
you just heard the situation applies also to kissing there is virus has been

01:16:06.010 --> 01:16:10.650
isolated from saliva we have no documented cases that were transmitted

01:16:10.650 --> 01:16:15.130
through kissing so we have to say the evidence is that there is no such

01:16:15.130 --> 01:16:19.270
transmission but we can't exclude the possibility that it can occur through

01:16:19.270 --> 01:16:24.740
kissing because there is virus virus in saliva in certain patients at least so

01:16:24.740 --> 01:16:29.000
kissing can occur but it has to be friendly superficial kissing

01:16:30.350 --> 01:16:35.890
And as to oral sex, it sounds to me as if the danger is certainly there, if there's

01:16:35.890 --> 01:16:40.320
any break in the skin, inside the mouth, or the gums, whatever.

01:16:40.320 --> 01:16:42.580
Yeah, and same thing with kissing.

01:16:42.580 --> 01:16:49.060
It's quite possible that 99% of times, kissing is not dangerous at all, but there is a possibility

01:16:49.060 --> 01:16:55.850
that somebody may have a break in the mucosa and his partner, his or her partner being infected,

01:16:55.850 --> 01:17:00.000
could bleed, and if all these circumstances are realized simultaneously,

01:17:00.000 --> 01:17:02.760
There is a theoretical possibility of infection.

01:17:02.980 --> 01:17:04.700
Now, Judy Woodruff talked about needles.

01:17:05.400 --> 01:17:07.260
Yes. This is very important.

01:17:07.680 --> 01:17:11.480
A very important mode of transmission is through contaminated needles,

01:17:11.720 --> 01:17:16.560
and this is the way the virus is transmitted in the drug-addicted community.

01:17:17.410 --> 01:17:20.070
Needles are very often not available to drug addicts.

01:17:20.070 --> 01:17:21.690
They have to buy them only.

01:17:22.170 --> 01:17:25.100
They must show a prescription to buy needles, so they don't have prescriptions.

01:17:25.840 --> 01:17:30.000
They have developed the habit of sharing a single needle among several people.

01:17:30.000 --> 01:17:35.360
in so-called drug alleys, and the needle goes from one vein to another, carrying a little

01:17:35.360 --> 01:17:36.360
bit of the blood.

01:17:36.360 --> 01:17:41.740
If one of the partners sharing the needle is contaminated, he will contaminate everybody

01:17:41.740 --> 01:17:43.300
else in the group.

01:17:43.300 --> 01:17:49.960
And transmission of the virus leading to AIDS has been very rapid in the addicted community,

01:17:49.960 --> 01:17:52.890
in New York in particular.

01:17:52.890 --> 01:17:57.230
And it's important to remember that this is the group that transmits the virus to the

01:17:57.230 --> 01:17:59.760
broader heterosexual community.

01:18:00.000 --> 01:18:04.230
because the drug addicts have by and large heterosexual people.

01:18:04.230 --> 01:18:10.540
And the virus, the infection, is transmitted to the population at large through them.

01:18:10.540 --> 01:18:17.630
So if we're talking about transmission to the heterosexual community,

01:18:17.630 --> 01:18:25.970
the avenues of transmission are through bisexual men who have sex with women and transmit to women.

01:18:25.970 --> 01:18:27.610
That's one possibility.

01:18:27.610 --> 01:18:30.000
And needle users who are female.

01:18:30.000 --> 01:18:31.000
No, also males.

01:18:31.000 --> 01:18:32.000
Male and female.

01:18:32.000 --> 01:18:33.000
And females.

01:18:33.000 --> 01:18:36.100
And most of them are males.

01:18:36.100 --> 01:18:42.880
And they can contract the infection through contaminated needles and pass it on to either

01:18:42.880 --> 01:18:45.480
needles or through sex to others.

01:18:45.480 --> 01:18:50.660
And then if the partners are females and these get infected, their children become infected,

01:18:50.660 --> 01:18:51.660
you know.

01:18:51.660 --> 01:18:55.920
There is also transmission in utero or at birth to an infant.

01:18:55.920 --> 01:19:00.000
So Dr. Wafsi, when we talk about groups at risk, what are we talking about?

01:19:00.000 --> 01:19:07.150
what groups are we talking about? Sounds like everybody. Potentially, everybody. It's always

01:19:07.150 --> 01:19:12.930
defined as homosexual males comprise the largest group, 70-some percent. Another 17 percent

01:19:12.930 --> 01:19:18.050
are IV drug users. A smaller group are hemophiliacs. Now that has been resolved by changing the

01:19:18.050 --> 01:19:23.420
nature of the materials, the anticoagulants that they're given. A smaller group than that

01:19:23.420 --> 01:19:30.000
has gotten AIDS via blood transfusion. That also has been addressed by testing of the

01:19:30.000 --> 01:19:36.200
group that's very small in percent, but it's growing slowly in number. And that's people

01:19:36.200 --> 01:19:41.940
who've gotten AIDS as a result of sexual activity alone. And that doesn't fall into a group.

01:19:42.280 --> 01:19:46.640
But I think we're naive if we think that everybody in a risk group has a label. I'm a gay male.

01:19:46.940 --> 01:19:52.560
I'm an IV drug user. I'm a hemophiliac. People don't look any particular part, and you can't tell.

01:19:52.560 --> 01:19:57.880
And the stereotypes of who looks like what or what socioeconomic group a person falls into

01:19:57.880 --> 01:20:00.000
isn't accurate, so you can't really tell

01:20:00.000 --> 01:20:06.980
who's in a group. Dr. Dowdle, do you have a sense of where this disease is going? We

01:20:06.980 --> 01:20:12.050
talk about these risk groups and from what Judy Woodruff said, it's at this point at

01:20:12.050 --> 01:20:17.760
least primarily a disease of the gay community. Where is it going?

01:20:17.760 --> 01:20:23.470
Dr. Well, certainly in Africa, the majority of the cases in Central Africa are heterosexual,

01:20:23.470 --> 01:20:29.060
heterosexually transmitted. There's no question about that. There's no doubt that heterosexual

01:20:29.060 --> 01:20:30.000
transmission will occur.

01:20:30.000 --> 01:20:34.140
are in this country. But the U.S. is not Africa, they're not the same practices, and it will

01:20:34.140 --> 01:20:38.780
not spread at the same rate. But there's no question that it will be very slowly spread

01:20:38.780 --> 01:20:40.180
unless precautions are taken.

01:20:40.180 --> 01:20:45.300
BILL MOYERS: All right, let's talk about precautions. Dr. Silverman, let me come

01:20:45.300 --> 01:20:52.040
back to you. There's the implication in what you've said about Fabian, about his being

01:20:52.040 --> 01:21:00.000
unusual, that if a person knows that they are a carrier of the AIDS virus, there might

01:21:00.000 --> 01:21:07.180
more likely to alter behavior and basically to behave carefully and that

01:21:07.180 --> 01:21:14.230
that leads us to testing I take it if if I'm to know whether I'm a carrier I

01:21:14.230 --> 01:21:22.660
need to take a test yes that's correct tell me about the test what is the test

01:21:22.660 --> 01:21:28.750
the test what happens to me suppose blood sample is drawn it is tested to

01:21:28.750 --> 01:21:30.000
see whether your body has

01:21:30.000 --> 01:21:35.880
responded to an infection with the HTLV3 or LAV virus or ARV depending on

01:21:35.880 --> 01:21:42.230
where you are and built antibodies to that virus and those antibodies are the

01:21:42.230 --> 01:21:46.790
tag or the signal or whatever that denotes the fact that you have been

01:21:46.790 --> 01:21:51.570
infected with this virus. It doesn't tell you whether you will get AIDS or

01:21:51.570 --> 01:21:55.290
whether you will get AIDS related complex. It just tells you that you have

01:21:55.290 --> 01:22:00.000
been infected and your body has responded. Now, I think that

01:22:00.000 --> 01:22:07.140
people who are concerned, who may be in the classic high-risk groups, should take the

01:22:07.140 --> 01:22:14.200
test if they have not altered their behavior, and if three caveats are obtained: one, that

01:22:14.200 --> 01:22:21.110
it's anonymous; two, that it's voluntary; and three, that there is extensive counseling

01:22:21.110 --> 01:22:23.650
before and after.

01:22:23.650 --> 01:22:25.210
Those three, I think, have to obtain.

01:22:25.210 --> 01:22:26.210
All right.

01:22:26.210 --> 01:22:27.710
Let me see about that.

01:22:27.710 --> 01:22:29.860
Dr. Dowdle, suppose I want to get a test.

01:22:30.640 --> 01:22:32.020
Where do I go to be tested?

01:22:32.020 --> 01:22:36.770
Well, the Public Health Service has recommended, in fact, that those in the high-risk group

01:22:36.770 --> 01:22:38.230
should voluntarily consider the test.

01:22:38.230 --> 01:22:41.980
I don't know that I'm in a high-risk group. I just, I want to be tested.

01:22:41.980 --> 01:22:47.120
Also, the recommendations are that these tests be provided at venereal disease clinics,

01:22:47.120 --> 01:22:48.980
as methadone clinics, et cetera.

01:22:48.980 --> 01:22:53.170
No, you mean I have to go to a venereal disease clinic if I want to be tested?

01:22:53.170 --> 01:22:58.170
No, almost every locality in almost every state has testing sites available which are

01:22:58.170 --> 01:23:00.000
generally well-known. In addition to that,

01:23:00.000 --> 01:23:02.640
that, you could go to your private physician and make arrangements.

01:23:02.640 --> 01:23:04.720
Dr. Raymond, I don't know where I get a test.

01:23:04.720 --> 01:23:06.320
I mean, I'm a reasonably well-informed person.

01:23:06.320 --> 01:23:07.880
I wouldn't have a clue where to go to get a test.

01:23:07.880 --> 01:23:10.720
Dr. You would call up your local health department or your state health department

01:23:10.720 --> 01:23:16.280
or AIDS hotlines, which are generally available in every city, but you can also go to your

01:23:16.280 --> 01:23:17.280
private physician.

01:23:17.280 --> 01:23:18.280
Dr. I go into a clinic.

01:23:18.280 --> 01:23:19.190
Dr. Yes.

01:23:19.190 --> 01:23:20.300
Dr. And then what happens to me?

01:23:20.300 --> 01:23:22.760
Dr. You could go into a clinic, and it depends on the state and depends on the locality

01:23:22.760 --> 01:23:29.140
as to what their laws are, but it's either confidential or it could be anonymous, depending

01:23:29.140 --> 01:23:30.000
on the particular location.

01:23:30.000 --> 01:23:31.620
Well, let's take that for starters.

01:23:31.620 --> 01:23:33.860
What happens to me physically?

01:23:33.860 --> 01:23:38.120
The recommendations are, and they're generally followed by every state and locality, that

01:23:38.120 --> 01:23:40.360
you come in first and are counseled.

01:23:40.360 --> 01:23:45.920
You are told what the test means, you're told what the results might mean, you're told whether

01:23:45.920 --> 01:23:48.620
you might be at risk or not, and do you want the test.

01:23:48.620 --> 01:23:50.700
If you still want the test, you're given the test.

01:23:50.700 --> 01:23:51.700
Yeah, I want the test.

01:23:51.700 --> 01:23:52.700
That's what I came for.

01:23:52.700 --> 01:23:55.800
Either with your name or without, depending on the state or the location.

01:23:55.800 --> 01:23:56.680
Is it pinprick?

01:23:56.680 --> 01:23:59.490
No, it would actually be, blood would be drawn from the arm.

01:23:59.490 --> 01:24:00.000
From the arm.

01:24:00.000 --> 01:24:05.600
just like um that's that's correct yeah and then uh how long before i find out again it depends on

01:24:05.600 --> 01:24:11.280
the location it depends upon the demand but it could be two days three days or so on and then

01:24:11.280 --> 01:24:17.270
there could be a second test if that test is positive how do i find out well you would come

01:24:17.270 --> 01:24:21.670
again depends on the location either you would be asked to come back at a particular time which is

01:24:21.670 --> 01:24:26.310
generally the way in which it's done and you would come back and you would be told that those were

01:24:26.310 --> 01:24:30.000
positive, if indeed they were positive, and they would like to do another confirmatory

01:24:30.000 --> 01:24:34.150
type of test and that would be done and then you would be you would come back

01:24:34.150 --> 01:24:38.410
again and be given the information but in each case counseling would be done

01:24:38.410 --> 01:24:42.200
you would not be informed by mail now what do you mean counseling counseling

01:24:42.200 --> 01:24:47.240
again indicating what the test means informing the individual what the test

01:24:47.240 --> 01:24:53.910
means whether or not that you wish to have the test what change in behavior

01:24:53.910 --> 01:24:58.410
that you might undergo if you indeed have a positive test or if you have a

01:24:58.410 --> 01:25:00.000
negative test.

01:25:00.000 --> 01:25:05.730
Suppose I show up positive, and I take the second test and I show up positive again.

01:25:05.730 --> 01:25:08.500
How long am I going to spend in this office?

01:25:08.500 --> 01:25:12.830
In the office, it could vary, 30 minutes or so.

01:25:12.830 --> 01:25:14.390
And that's when I'm counseled?

01:25:14.390 --> 01:25:17.310
That's during the counseling period, yes, that would be correct.

01:25:17.310 --> 01:25:18.690
And what after that?

01:25:18.690 --> 01:25:23.610
Well, after that, if you have a positive test, then you're informed as to what action you

01:25:23.610 --> 01:25:28.200
might take to prevent transmitting the disease to others or the virus infection to others.

01:25:28.200 --> 01:25:29.200
Go ahead and inform me.

01:25:29.200 --> 01:25:30.000
Or how you might...

01:25:30.060 --> 01:25:33.790
change your own behavior. Inform me. I want to know. The

01:25:33.790 --> 01:25:37.700
recommendations that would be given to you, if you were positive,

01:25:38.340 --> 01:25:41.960
they would, such things as do not have, avoiding sex

01:25:41.960 --> 01:25:45.190
altogether is the first way in which you can obviously

01:25:45.190 --> 01:25:49.380
avoid transmitting it. On the other hand, if

01:25:49.380 --> 01:25:53.590
that's not always likely, we recognize that, therefore

01:25:53.590 --> 01:25:56.610
the use of condoms are some protection.

01:25:57.270 --> 01:26:00.000
The do not, for example, share such

01:26:00.000 --> 01:26:06.500
things as razors or any materials where you might be sharing blood and do not share toothbrushes

01:26:06.500 --> 01:26:08.620
and so on and so forth.

01:26:08.620 --> 01:26:11.990
So there are recommendations in this type of line.

01:26:11.990 --> 01:26:17.030
And Dr. Vernon, do I get counseling beyond that?

01:26:17.030 --> 01:26:18.030
That is, is there follow-up?

01:26:18.030 --> 01:26:20.980
Am I put into a program?

01:26:20.980 --> 01:26:24.790
Is there a support system that automatically takes over?

01:26:24.790 --> 01:26:30.000
In virtually every community, there's a support system that is primarily run by the

01:26:30.000 --> 01:26:33.250
The gay community itself, certainly in our state, that is the case.

01:26:33.990 --> 01:26:35.290
But what happens if I'm not gay?

01:26:35.860 --> 01:26:43.870
Well, if you're not gay, you're going to get extensive counseling from the public health people about whatever risk factors you may have.

01:26:44.490 --> 01:26:49.450
If you're a hemophiliac, you're very likely not to be involved with public health at all,

01:26:49.510 --> 01:26:53.150
but with the medical people who are caring for you routinely.

01:26:54.200 --> 01:27:00.000
But the point is that that counseling is the critical moment in this day,

01:27:00.000 --> 01:27:06.040
in age in terms of our ability to control the epidemic of the HDLV3 virus.

01:27:06.040 --> 01:27:09.920
Dr. Silverman, you stressed "voluntary."

01:27:09.920 --> 01:27:11.160
Absolutely.

01:27:11.160 --> 01:27:16.500
As I've heard it so far, I take this test and all it is is bad news.

01:27:16.500 --> 01:27:18.170
Or it could be good news.

01:27:18.170 --> 01:27:19.360
It could be good news.

01:27:19.360 --> 01:27:21.780
That is, you could tell me I don't have the virus.

01:27:21.780 --> 01:27:26.930
And then I would tell you how to make sure you don't get the virus.

01:27:26.930 --> 01:27:30.000
But if you test me positive, that's just total bad news.

01:27:30.090 --> 01:27:31.550
Well, it isn't total bad news

01:27:31.550 --> 01:27:35.650
because you're equating a positive test with AIDS.

01:27:36.050 --> 01:27:38.730
The positive test is equated with infection.

01:27:39.230 --> 01:27:42.170
Infection is in the early part of a process

01:27:42.170 --> 01:27:43.790
which may not go on to AIDS,

01:27:44.070 --> 01:27:46.050
may not go on to AIDS-related complex,

01:27:46.270 --> 01:27:48.510
may just be that you've been infected,

01:27:48.850 --> 01:27:50.430
somehow your body has dealt with it,

01:27:50.630 --> 01:27:52.150
and that is not a problem.

01:27:52.230 --> 01:27:53.730
What we can do for you, though...

01:27:53.730 --> 01:27:55.210
But I gather the chances are pretty good.

01:27:56.180 --> 01:27:57.450
No, we don't know.

01:27:57.960 --> 01:28:00.000
We think probably in the range

01:28:00.000 --> 01:28:05.450
of 30 to 40 percent may go on to get AIDS. This is again somewhat speculation, but we

01:28:05.450 --> 01:28:10.790
see people who have tested positive for several years who are doing very well. We don't know

01:28:10.790 --> 01:28:15.940
of any disease where there's 100 percent infection going on to disease. Here's my question.

01:28:16.850 --> 01:28:22.210
Why do I, I mean, why do I want to take this test? It sounds to me like you're either going

01:28:22.210 --> 01:28:27.160
to tell me I don't have it, which is great, or you're going to tell me I have it, in which

01:28:27.160 --> 01:28:30.000
case there's nothing much I can do. No, there's a great deal you can

01:28:30.000 --> 01:28:34.120
do. You have a responsibility to yourself and to society.

01:28:34.120 --> 01:28:37.790
You mean there's something I can do for everyone else? What can I do for me?

01:28:37.790 --> 01:28:41.630
Well, let's talk about you for a minute. You said you're straight, you're not gay.

01:28:41.630 --> 01:28:45.610
If you're positive, you have a spouse. You have a spouse that may be planning, the two

01:28:45.610 --> 01:28:51.380
of you, to have a child. That is very important information for you, for your wife, for your

01:28:51.380 --> 01:28:55.990
unborn child. Very important information. Now, maybe we will be able to do something

01:28:55.990 --> 01:29:00.000
which will eliminate that infection from you in the future, and you can go on to have a

01:29:00.000 --> 01:29:01.860
we'd counsel you against that.

01:29:01.860 --> 01:29:03.940
That's very important information for you.

01:29:03.940 --> 01:29:06.480
We would want you to stay as healthy as possible.

01:29:06.480 --> 01:29:09.440
We know that stress, we know that poor eating habits

01:29:09.440 --> 01:29:12.060
and lack of rest and lack of exercise

01:29:12.060 --> 01:29:13.580
does not help the immune system.

01:29:13.580 --> 01:29:15.240
It impairs the immune system.

01:29:15.240 --> 01:29:17.740
We can work with you to improve your health

01:29:17.740 --> 01:29:19.950
to the degree possible,

01:29:19.950 --> 01:29:22.190
but we're not giving you a death sentence.

01:29:22.190 --> 01:29:23.690
We may be giving you a death sentence

01:29:23.690 --> 01:29:25.530
with the diagnosis of AIDS.

01:29:25.530 --> 01:29:27.470
Unfortunately, that seems so.

01:29:27.470 --> 01:29:29.860
But there's no death sentence with the infection.

01:29:30.120 --> 01:29:32.300
That is just one piece of information.

01:29:32.300 --> 01:29:35.880
Now, granted, there are some individuals who shouldn't take the test

01:29:35.880 --> 01:29:40.570
because that information would be enough to throw them over the edge.

01:29:40.670 --> 01:29:45.470
In other words, they're labile personalities, and they might commit suicide, might do something.

01:29:45.570 --> 01:29:46.250
What kind of personality?

01:29:46.510 --> 01:29:46.990
Labile.

01:29:47.400 --> 01:29:48.520
Labile. I don't know that.

01:29:48.980 --> 01:29:57.510
Well, that their emotions are such that they could go over the line, if you will, and take very drastic action.

01:29:57.510 --> 01:30:00.000
I mean, I've talked to some gay men who said,

01:30:00.220 --> 01:30:04.660
following safe sex practices I don't need that information and if I knew I had

01:30:04.660 --> 01:30:13.690
it I might commit suicide I'm sitting here hemorrhaging we're talking about

01:30:13.690 --> 01:30:17.370
the responsibility of public health officials in this country to be able to

01:30:17.370 --> 01:30:23.900
allow counseling to take place for this kind of problem HIV testing I think

01:30:23.900 --> 01:30:27.570
Houston is a clear example of a lack of responsibility of the public health

01:30:27.570 --> 01:30:30.000
officials in that city and many other cities in this

01:30:30.000 --> 01:30:34.260
country that they're not going to be able to handle the difficulties around

01:30:34.260 --> 01:30:38.580
counseling and the issue of exposure and what that means and what it doesn't mean

01:30:38.580 --> 01:30:42.600
that's one thing too I think what dr. Superman just mentioned is a very

01:30:42.600 --> 01:30:48.480
isolated case there are many people I know we've treated a GMHC over 3,000

01:30:48.480 --> 01:30:53.710
clients not one of them presented some of the issues that came out were

01:30:53.710 --> 01:31:00.000
presented in today's documentary not very few of them talked about suicide

01:31:00.000 --> 01:31:02.240
as a viable option.

01:31:02.910 --> 01:31:06.370
In fact, they talked more about regaining control in their lies

01:31:06.370 --> 01:31:09.570
and responding to their anger in a responsible way

01:31:09.570 --> 01:31:12.350
so that something could come out of the feelings of anger.

01:31:12.350 --> 01:31:15.330
But are you telling me that there's really no problem

01:31:15.330 --> 01:31:18.980
if you offer testing, people will flock to it?

01:31:19.210 --> 01:31:20.150
I don't think so.

01:31:20.650 --> 01:31:23.970
I think it depends on the kinds of information the public has

01:31:23.970 --> 01:31:25.540
and the kind of education they get.

01:31:25.540 --> 01:31:28.800
If they realize that knowing whether you're positive or negative

01:31:28.800 --> 01:31:30.000
can

01:31:30.000 --> 01:31:34.500
can't tell you if you're gonna get this disease number one number two I don't see

01:31:34.500 --> 01:31:39.120
how in the name of good conscience and ethics that this country is going to

01:31:39.120 --> 01:31:43.600
respond with the appropriate counseling needs of our population they haven't up

01:31:43.600 --> 01:31:47.400
to date Houston is a very I gotta keep going back there because it's a very

01:31:47.400 --> 01:31:51.120
clear example of I think what would happen here the lack of education of our

01:31:51.120 --> 01:31:57.490
public health officials is is a is a criminal it's criminal what happened to

01:31:57.490 --> 01:32:00.000
to to to Fabian was

01:32:00.000 --> 01:32:04.910
was criminal, okay? The way he was victimized was criminal. And I think that's typical of

01:32:04.910 --> 01:32:08.930
the way public health officials in this country will respond. I think they will not want to

01:32:08.930 --> 01:32:11.730
know because of their own difficulties in dealing with all the issues.

01:32:11.730 --> 01:32:19.390
Let me go to a public health official. Dr. Vernon, your testing in Colorado, I understand

01:32:19.390 --> 01:32:21.110
is not mandatory.

01:32:21.110 --> 01:32:22.690
Absolutely not.

01:32:22.690 --> 01:32:23.690
But not anonymous?

01:32:23.690 --> 01:32:25.480
Not anonymous. Right.

01:32:25.480 --> 01:32:28.470
Now, Dr. Silverman says you've got to have it anonymous.

01:32:28.470 --> 01:32:30.000
We disagree. We have it.

01:32:30.000 --> 01:32:40.920
I happen to believe that the confidentiality protections that exist in statute and regulation in Colorado make it unnecessary for us to attempt to do disease control anonymously.

01:32:40.920 --> 01:32:45.950
We think of the individuals that we can't reach with counseling because we don't know how to reach them.

01:32:45.950 --> 01:32:51.900
We think of the individuals whom we may need to reach in the future, whom we could not reach if we did not have the information.

01:32:51.900 --> 01:32:53.880
So you want to follow up on these people?

01:32:53.880 --> 01:33:00.000
We want to follow up when there comes an opportunity for them to get a vaccine or a drug or some other benefit.

01:33:00.000 --> 01:33:00.680
that is available.

01:33:01.310 --> 01:33:05.270
Yes, everyone says they will come out of the woodwork, they will all be there, but we know

01:33:05.270 --> 01:33:06.890
differently from previous behavior.

01:33:06.890 --> 01:33:12.550
We have an opportunity because of a confidential medical record system to reach individuals.

01:33:13.240 --> 01:33:16.780
Now, why is Dr. Silverman so insistent on anonymity?

01:33:17.000 --> 01:33:25.080
I hope he is insistent on anonymity being available in some way as an option, in some

01:33:25.080 --> 01:33:30.000
form, so that individuals would be able, would be encouraged to get the test who would

01:33:30.000 --> 01:33:36.950
get it. We agree that the important thing is being tested. Unfortunately, gay leadership

01:33:36.950 --> 01:33:41.840
in this country is still saying that the test is not useful. Many are saying that it should

01:33:41.840 --> 01:33:44.840
not be obtained, and we totally disagree with that.

01:33:44.840 --> 01:33:50.570
Let me go to Denver. Mr. Rush? Can you hear me, Mr. Rush?

01:33:50.570 --> 01:33:52.310
Yes, I can.

01:33:52.310 --> 01:33:57.940
Mr. Rush, Dr. Vernon runs a system of testing which is not anonymous.

01:33:57.940 --> 01:33:59.000
That's correct.

01:33:59.000 --> 01:34:00.000
Do you trust it?

01:34:01.050 --> 01:34:08.970
I can't speak, I can't be presumptuous enough to speak for the whole gay community, but there are many, many people here that don't feel good about that at all.

01:34:08.970 --> 01:34:17.130
We feel that there would be many more people who would be willing to come forward and be tested if they chose to, if we didn't have reportability.

01:34:17.130 --> 01:34:26.170
At this point, I think it's important to note, too, that we're not sure that there's any correlation between being tested and changing behavior.

01:34:26.170 --> 01:34:29.830
So I think that's another thing that, you know, we need to look at on down the line.

01:34:30.570 --> 01:34:33.780
Mr. Holloway, can I switch to you?

01:34:33.780 --> 01:34:35.440
Yes.

01:34:35.440 --> 01:34:37.290
Mr. Holloway, do you trust it?

01:34:37.290 --> 01:34:43.390
I do not trust the actual confidentiality,

01:34:43.390 --> 01:34:47.060
even though it has never been broken.

01:34:47.060 --> 01:34:51.970
And the reason is this: that I believe that the strength of the gay community,

01:34:51.970 --> 01:34:57.170
the compassion, if you please, if it is applied to the gay community

01:34:57.170 --> 01:35:00.000
and we all work together, that we will be much better educated

01:35:00.000 --> 01:35:06.610
educated, we will get the test, we will know our situation, and just as we saw in the Houston

01:35:06.610 --> 01:35:13.210
situation, the compassionate intervention of the gay community is the key to it.

01:35:13.210 --> 01:35:17.490
When other people, when health officials and government officials could not be successful,

01:35:17.490 --> 01:35:19.100
the gay community could.

01:35:19.100 --> 01:35:25.190
The gay community in Colorado is saying to us, we must have anonymous testing if we're

01:35:25.190 --> 01:35:30.000
going to cooperate, if we're going to really find out about this disease, and be successful.

01:35:30.000 --> 01:35:37.820
in curbing the disease. Prevention and education have to go together. And I want to point out in

01:35:37.820 --> 01:35:45.040
relationship to what Mr. Lopez said, that many people who are being supported in our support

01:35:45.040 --> 01:35:51.590
groups here in Colorado are being supported not only by gay members of the community, but by other

01:35:51.590 --> 01:35:57.980
people, by people who are parents, who are concerned citizens. So I think our system here,

01:35:57.980 --> 01:36:00.000
If a person is tested,

01:36:00.120 --> 01:36:02.000
they find they are positive

01:36:02.000 --> 01:36:03.260
and they're frightened

01:36:03.260 --> 01:36:07.810
as we all are when we find out this drastic news

01:36:07.810 --> 01:36:09.510
there is a support system

01:36:09.510 --> 01:36:12.830
i think the health departments and government officials have to learn to

01:36:12.830 --> 01:36:15.110
creatively work with the gay community

01:36:15.110 --> 01:36:19.350
we haven't yet done that and we must if we're going to be successful

01:36:19.350 --> 01:36:22.340
thank you mr holloway

01:36:22.340 --> 01:36:23.750
there's also an issue

01:36:23.750 --> 01:36:26.760
there's a fallacy here about confidentiality

01:36:26.760 --> 01:36:29.760
i just recently got out of a hospital

01:36:30.000 --> 01:36:35.060
When I was taken into the elevator, and I'm just one person, in my experience, I was put

01:36:35.060 --> 01:36:41.530
in the elevator, medical people were discussing the case of two patients in that hospital

01:36:41.530 --> 01:36:47.950
used their names in the elevator, okay, a number of people came up to me in the corridors

01:36:47.950 --> 01:36:52.250
of that hospital and wanted to share personal experiences of what they felt and thought

01:36:52.250 --> 01:36:54.990
about the conditions of certain people in that place.

01:36:55.290 --> 01:36:56.930
There was no confidentiality.

01:36:57.440 --> 01:37:00.000
I mean, confidentiality was being broken by everyone in that

01:37:00.000 --> 01:37:05.360
entire system, and I think it's a fallacy to think that it's going to be observed by

01:37:05.360 --> 01:37:10.760
all the systems in this country. The reality is that, as we've seen, just Houston is only

01:37:10.760 --> 01:37:16.170
one example. I think Dallas is another example. You look across the board to the issues that

01:37:16.170 --> 01:37:19.370
people have, and you look across the board to the concerns people have about putting

01:37:19.370 --> 01:37:24.130
themselves personally on the line, and confidentiality will not be safeguarded. For Fabian, they

01:37:24.130 --> 01:37:29.310
certainly were not. Mr. Yates-Rist, you have a reaction. I think one of the things we're avoiding

01:37:29.310 --> 01:37:30.000
here is something

01:37:30.000 --> 01:37:37.500
And it goes way underneath, it lies way underneath all of the discussions of quarantine with Mr. Dan Meyer, Mr. Vernon's testing, Mr. Silverman's testing.

01:37:38.120 --> 01:37:44.700
And that is, first of all, when you're talking about testing and knowing your antibody status,

01:37:45.240 --> 01:37:50.680
the counseling they're offering is going to give us nothing that education doesn't give us already.

01:37:50.680 --> 01:37:56.820
Instead of wasting our time and money in this country, which we have very little of for

01:37:56.820 --> 01:38:00.000
health currently under the Reagan administration.

01:38:00.000 --> 01:38:04.740
things why aren't we spending all of this money on education we know it works

01:38:04.740 --> 01:38:09.540
because it's worked in New York City there is as much as an 85% drop in

01:38:09.540 --> 01:38:13.500
venereal disease rates in New York City but there's something beyond this and

01:38:13.500 --> 01:38:18.680
it's the same statistic that I think dr. Silverman was advice and may I just say

01:38:18.680 --> 01:38:23.120
that studies have shown in the testing in San Francisco a significant change of

01:38:23.120 --> 01:38:28.270
behavior as a result of testing as stated by those who were tested well I

01:38:28.270 --> 01:38:30.000
I would like to know how much better you could

01:38:30.000 --> 01:38:34.720
than 85 percent and we don't have testing in new york but let me make another point because this is

01:38:34.720 --> 01:38:41.190
a point that's being avoided all evening uh and that is you're asking us to let the government

01:38:41.190 --> 01:38:47.350
come into our lives to test to quarantine and we're avoiding the whole issue of how much the

01:38:47.350 --> 01:38:54.720
society hates homosexuals we heard it on on tv from dr hotzi tonight who has to say it's inordinate

01:38:54.720 --> 01:39:00.000
lust, it's anonymous sex. He wants to avoid the truth of homosexuality which is it's a

01:39:00.000 --> 01:39:04.740
love and relationships every bit as much as heterosexuality is, but that's not

01:39:04.740 --> 01:39:09.180
what people want to hear. And when we have homophobic people in our government

01:39:09.180 --> 01:39:15.730
ready to climb down our throats at any minute to destroy the gay community, why

01:39:15.730 --> 01:39:19.810
should we trust the government? Why should we trust Senator Dannemeyer? Is he

01:39:19.810 --> 01:39:23.430
going to protect, is he going to protect the right of homosexuals to live freely in

01:39:23.430 --> 01:39:30.000
this society? May I respond to that? Yes, Congressman. You see, one thing you may be overlooking is that the founding

01:39:30.000 --> 01:39:38.920
foundation of Western Civilization, the Judeo-Christian ethic teaches us that God's plan for man is

01:39:38.920 --> 01:39:42.680
one man and one woman who come together and form a family unit.

01:39:42.680 --> 01:39:49.120
Excuse me, I really don't want to hear about what you said, I am a homosexual.

01:39:49.120 --> 01:39:51.820
Mr. Yates risk, he's absolutely right.

01:39:51.820 --> 01:39:52.820
He didn't interrupt you.

01:39:52.820 --> 01:39:53.840
I didn't interrupt you.

01:39:53.840 --> 01:40:00.000
And I can tell you, my friend, that I will, so long as I'm permitted to be in public office

01:40:00.000 --> 01:40:10.130
Even after I'm retired from public office, I will affirm the support, the affirmation of the heterosexual ethic unapologetically.

01:40:10.460 --> 01:40:10.920
Now, wait a minute.

01:40:11.180 --> 01:40:11.740
That doesn't mean...

01:40:11.740 --> 01:40:13.260
We got nothing against you doing that.

01:40:13.500 --> 01:40:16.840
But his problem is that there's a downside to what you say.

01:40:16.980 --> 01:40:19.200
It sounds like you're the homophobe that he's talking about.

01:40:19.200 --> 01:40:19.640
No, no, listen.

01:40:20.020 --> 01:40:22.840
I affirm a support for a heterosexual ethic.

01:40:22.840 --> 01:40:24.420
How about affirming a support for a homosexual?

01:40:24.960 --> 01:40:27.260
And naturally, those two are in conflict.

01:40:27.780 --> 01:40:30.000
And I am not about to apologize

01:40:30.000 --> 01:40:33.680
Since it's my life he's talking about, I would like to interrupt

01:40:33.680 --> 01:40:37.400
because it's his kind who have interrupted homosexuals for our whole lives

01:40:37.400 --> 01:40:38.860
and will try to speak for ourselves.

01:40:39.160 --> 01:40:40.680
Now, I'd like to pick up on this.

01:40:40.680 --> 01:40:43.120
It's only going to work if it's one at a time, all right?

01:40:43.860 --> 01:40:46.360
I am 38 years old.

01:40:46.700 --> 01:40:49.520
I am in a relationship which is stable and beautiful,

01:40:49.700 --> 01:40:53.680
and it's something that is available to every homosexual man and woman in this country

01:40:53.680 --> 01:40:55.660
if people like you will leave us alone.

01:40:55.960 --> 01:40:59.060
But as long as you are out there setting public policy

01:40:59.060 --> 01:41:00.000
and determine

01:41:00.000 --> 01:41:03.360
I'm determining exactly the way this disease is going to be treated by the government.

01:41:03.360 --> 01:41:09.460
I will not trust the government and I urge every gay man and woman out there to rebel

01:41:09.460 --> 01:41:14.670
against any impulse of this government to get into our lives.

01:41:14.670 --> 01:41:19.350
If we trust you, we'll be ridden down the river and let everyone be aware of it.

01:41:19.350 --> 01:41:20.690
All right, now it's my turn to interrupt.

01:41:20.690 --> 01:41:21.600
May I respond to that?

01:41:21.600 --> 01:41:24.410
No.

01:41:24.410 --> 01:41:25.540
I'll tell you what my concern is.

01:41:25.540 --> 01:41:27.840
We've talked about the homosexual aspect of this.

01:41:30.540 --> 01:41:36.280
Let's assume I'm a father of a daughter who is 12 years old.

01:41:36.280 --> 01:41:43.250
Dr. Wofsi, does any of what's happened here, discussed here tonight, relate to me?

01:41:43.250 --> 01:41:44.470
Do I have anything to worry about?

01:41:44.470 --> 01:41:49.760
Dr. I listen to all of this as an infectious disease specialist.

01:41:49.760 --> 01:41:56.810
I realize we're talking about an infectious disease, and that should be unrelated to color

01:41:56.810 --> 01:42:00.000
or sexual preference.

01:42:00.000 --> 01:42:05.660
very irritating to hear all of this going back and forth 25% of people who have AIDS

01:42:05.660 --> 01:42:11.630
and possibly a greater percent of all those that carry the virus are not homosexual it's

01:42:11.630 --> 01:42:16.280
an infectious disease that affects a variety of people does a father of a 12 year old child

01:42:16.280 --> 01:42:23.210
have something to be concerned about very very very little however I don't need to worry

01:42:23.210 --> 01:42:30.000
about my daughter AIDS in some way or another is going to affect everybody in the United

01:42:30.000 --> 01:42:35.530
in the next several years and I don't mean by direct risk to themselves but by

01:42:35.530 --> 01:42:40.990
their contacts or their associates as far as having a child be it male a male

01:42:40.990 --> 01:42:45.850
child or a female child a boy or a girl who is entering the years of sexual

01:42:45.850 --> 01:42:51.420
experimentation a boy may find out that he's gay and it's like a lot of other

01:42:51.420 --> 01:42:55.940
things in society that have been sort of kept under covers child abuse etc it's

01:42:55.940 --> 01:43:00.000
been going on we just we just don't realize that there are a large percent of

01:43:00.000 --> 01:43:04.090
of a relatively large percent of the population that is gay.

01:43:04.090 --> 01:43:06.320
That's just the way they are.

01:43:06.320 --> 01:43:12.150
And I think that there's probably been inhibition of boys in their teenage years who are afraid

01:43:12.150 --> 01:43:16.590
to express this and may experiment without the advice and counsel.

01:43:16.590 --> 01:43:21.470
For a 12-year-old girl, I doubt that most 12-year-old girls are sexually active, but

01:43:21.470 --> 01:43:24.000
there may be some who are.

01:43:24.000 --> 01:43:30.000
And as the years go on and the number of cases increases, we have to educate everybody in

01:43:30.000 --> 01:43:35.680
perfectly reasonable way without being afraid to talk about sex or pretend that it isn't

01:43:35.680 --> 01:43:41.060
a normal part of life and just discuss AIDS, that AIDS is part of our society and sexuality

01:43:41.060 --> 01:43:47.080
is something that people should be comfortable with and that there are diseases people can

01:43:47.080 --> 01:43:48.080
get through sex.

01:43:48.080 --> 01:43:49.080
All right.

01:43:49.080 --> 01:43:50.080
So let's do it.

01:43:50.080 --> 01:43:51.080
Let's do it.

01:43:51.080 --> 01:43:56.100
Let's assume my daughter is 14 and my son is 16 and maybe I'm a little out of touch with

01:43:56.100 --> 01:43:57.100
them.

01:43:57.100 --> 01:44:00.000
Maybe I don't know exactly what goes on in some parts of their lives.

01:44:01.470 --> 01:44:05.360
Do I counsel them? Is that the choice? Do they get it someplace else?

01:44:05.360 --> 01:44:08.260
The parent is best. But if the parent doesn't know or isn't comfortable...

01:44:08.260 --> 01:44:10.670
Right, now what do I tell them? What do I tell them?

01:44:10.670 --> 01:44:15.900
You start by trying to be at ease with the issue of sexuality and realizing...

01:44:15.900 --> 01:44:18.240
Alright, I'm relaxed. I'm at ease. Now what do I tell them?

01:44:18.240 --> 01:44:24.310
Okay. You tell them that there are diseases that people can get from having sex.

01:44:24.310 --> 01:44:27.250
And some of them are easy to cure and some of them aren't.

01:44:27.250 --> 01:44:29.760
And you don't know very much about certain of those diseases.

01:44:30.000 --> 01:44:32.020
and you want to be sure they get information.

01:44:32.020 --> 01:44:34.470
And so you find whatever your community has

01:44:34.470 --> 01:44:36.950
that they can get the information.

01:44:36.950 --> 01:44:39.990
You endorse education in the schools

01:44:39.990 --> 01:44:42.220
so that it's not treated as a big deal.

01:44:42.220 --> 01:44:43.800
It's just something that's there.

01:44:43.800 --> 01:44:47.600
We have to learn about not taking candy from strangers.

01:44:47.600 --> 01:44:49.000
We have to learn to look right and left

01:44:49.000 --> 01:44:49.840
when we cross the street.

01:44:49.840 --> 01:44:50.780
We have to learn to put on a seatbelt.

01:44:50.780 --> 01:44:53.680
We have to learn about sexuality and using condoms

01:44:53.680 --> 01:44:54.760
if that's appropriate.

01:44:54.760 --> 01:44:56.520
We have to learn all those things.

01:44:56.520 --> 01:44:57.940
Go slow on that one.

01:44:57.940 --> 01:45:00.000
We're going to learn that in school, that is how to use condoms

01:45:00.000 --> 01:45:03.000
and sex?

01:45:03.000 --> 01:45:07.200
You have to learn that that's a subject that has to be approached.

01:45:07.200 --> 01:45:13.610
Young people in high school, and in some instances in junior high school, are sexually active.

01:45:13.610 --> 01:45:17.370
And it's pulling the wool over our eyes to say that because we don't want it to happen,

01:45:17.370 --> 01:45:21.370
either on religious grounds or moral grounds, or because we're afraid of diseases, or because

01:45:21.370 --> 01:45:24.480
it offends us, it's happening.

01:45:24.480 --> 01:45:28.190
And if there's a good relationship parent to child, you can explain what the issues are

01:45:28.190 --> 01:45:30.000
about.

01:45:30.000 --> 01:45:34.740
the child as a mature person, but stop putting your head in the sand.

01:45:34.740 --> 01:45:37.080
Do I need to tell my children about needles, too?

01:45:37.080 --> 01:45:39.000
Yes.

01:45:39.000 --> 01:45:40.540
Dr. Krim, do I need to tell them about needles?

01:45:40.540 --> 01:45:42.700
Yes, you can tell your children about needles.

01:45:42.700 --> 01:45:43.700
Use clean needles, kids.

01:45:43.700 --> 01:45:44.700
No.

01:45:44.700 --> 01:45:45.700
Make sure you use clean needles.

01:45:45.700 --> 01:45:46.720
No, no, no, no.

01:45:46.720 --> 01:45:52.340
You start through the biology, as with the sex, you have to know about the disease, the

01:45:52.340 --> 01:45:54.550
virus, the transmission, and so forth.

01:45:54.550 --> 01:45:58.970
And then the role of the drug culture and the dirty needles in the transmission of the

01:45:58.970 --> 01:46:00.000
disease.

01:46:00.000 --> 01:46:06.220
being given a reason to avoid a certain danger and then in addition I would not

01:46:06.220 --> 01:46:09.840
only talk to the children about the dirty needles but to our government

01:46:09.840 --> 01:46:14.680
representatives that to deny the availability of clean needles to drug

01:46:14.680 --> 01:46:20.040
addicts is virtually to sentence a certain number of people to die nowadays

01:46:20.040 --> 01:46:24.180
and that laws have to be changed with this in this regard. Now if I'm a parent

01:46:24.180 --> 01:46:30.000
who's too too tight to talk about sex and needles and drugs with my kids

01:46:30.060 --> 01:46:35.240
Well then there are psychologists, counselors, there are other people who can do it.

01:46:35.240 --> 01:46:36.240
But it must be done.

01:46:36.240 --> 01:46:37.240
Somebody must do it.

01:46:37.240 --> 01:46:40.050
Does it need to be done in the schools?

01:46:40.050 --> 01:46:41.050
I think so.

01:46:41.050 --> 01:46:42.130
I think it's a good place also.

01:46:42.130 --> 01:46:45.560
Congressman Dannemeyer, is it going to be done in the schools?

01:46:45.560 --> 01:46:47.520
Well, I'd like to come back to this other topic.

01:46:47.520 --> 01:46:48.520
No, no.

01:46:48.520 --> 01:46:49.520
I want this one.

01:46:49.520 --> 01:46:50.880
Is it going to be done in the schools?

01:46:50.880 --> 01:46:55.510
I believe that a school board in our system, we believe in local control in school districts

01:46:55.510 --> 01:47:00.000
of America, has to make a decision as to what type of subjects will

01:47:00.000 --> 01:47:04.360
It will be taught in the curriculum, and that decision is going to be answered in different

01:47:04.360 --> 01:47:06.560
ways in school boards across the country.

01:47:06.560 --> 01:47:11.760
I don't think that we should be making a blanket, certainly not at the federal level, we should

01:47:11.760 --> 01:47:16.440
not be making a blanket law with respect to what should be taught on the issue of sexuality

01:47:16.440 --> 01:47:18.060
or drugs in every school district in America.

01:47:18.060 --> 01:47:21.530
You don't think there's an issue on which we need federal leadership?

01:47:21.530 --> 01:47:25.470
I think there are areas where federal leadership is called for.

01:47:25.470 --> 01:47:29.060
I've introduced five pieces of legislation, and I'd like to respond to my friend, if I

01:47:29.060 --> 01:47:30.000
may.

01:47:30.000 --> 01:47:32.240
No, no, no, no. You're not playing fair with me, Congressman.

01:47:32.240 --> 01:47:32.640
I'd like to.

01:47:32.640 --> 01:47:33.740
You're just not playing fair with me.

01:47:33.820 --> 01:47:34.460
I think I should.

01:47:34.880 --> 01:47:41.630
What two men or two women or a man and a woman do in the privacy of their own home is none of my business.

01:47:41.750 --> 01:47:43.130
It's none of the government's business.

01:47:43.500 --> 01:47:49.310
But when those two men come out of their privacy of their home and they come into the public sector where I work

01:47:49.310 --> 01:47:56.460
and they want to change the 1964 Federal Civil Rights Act so as to include sexual preference

01:47:56.460 --> 01:48:00.000
as something that it would be an enforceable federal

01:48:00.000 --> 01:48:01.930
Civil Rights Act, they've got

01:48:01.930 --> 01:48:04.060
my attention. Because at that point

01:48:04.060 --> 01:48:05.980
they are seeking to use the

01:48:05.980 --> 01:48:08.220
federal law as a means

01:48:08.220 --> 01:48:09.880
of changing the basic

01:48:09.880 --> 01:48:11.860
culture of America so as

01:48:11.860 --> 01:48:14.200
to equate the homosexual lifestyle

01:48:14.200 --> 01:48:15.920
on a par with the heterosexual

01:48:15.920 --> 01:48:17.900
lifestyle. And at that point

01:48:17.900 --> 01:48:19.400
they've got my attention.

01:48:19.400 --> 01:48:21.600
You guys can handle this after this is over, alright?

01:48:21.780 --> 01:48:24.220
I'll set up a private discussion for you, alright?

01:48:24.760 --> 01:48:26.240
I'm interested in knowing

01:48:26.240 --> 01:48:27.780
what's going to happen to my kids.

01:48:29.120 --> 01:48:30.000
I'm curious

01:48:30.000 --> 01:48:35.860
about that I want to know is some guy somebody gonna tell my kids about needles

01:48:35.860 --> 01:48:43.950
and condoms I want to know I tell you what I want to know miss McLaughlin is

01:48:43.950 --> 01:48:54.570
somebody going to is somebody gonna go even further than that you see any you

01:48:54.570 --> 01:48:59.410
see any any future in making needles free to people

01:49:00.190 --> 01:49:01.190
Well, I speak as a...

01:49:01.190 --> 01:49:02.190
Were condoms free to people?

01:49:02.190 --> 01:49:09.420
Oh, I speak as a pragmatist, however beneficial I think it might be to distribute free needles.

01:49:09.420 --> 01:49:10.720
It's not going to sell.

01:49:10.720 --> 01:49:13.930
The public isn't going to accept it.

01:49:13.930 --> 01:49:17.080
I think a lot more could be done with condoms.

01:49:17.080 --> 01:49:19.980
But I think I would like to say something about what I've heard.

01:49:19.980 --> 01:49:22.660
Let me just stop on that for a minute.

01:49:22.660 --> 01:49:24.480
I hear a ring of reality to what you say.

01:49:24.480 --> 01:49:28.740
I'm not doubting it as things stand at the moment.

01:49:32.360 --> 01:49:38.660
Imagine the clock turned forward so that the numbers on that pyramid get bigger.

01:49:40.780 --> 01:49:46.310
Is it possible that the public will come around to a point where they see that this thing is on us

01:49:46.310 --> 01:49:48.900
and we've got to do something about it?

01:49:50.260 --> 01:49:52.950
I feel the clock is going to go forward.

01:49:52.950 --> 01:50:00.000
But I think before the public will accept the distribution of free needles for democracy,

01:50:00.000 --> 01:50:09.400
drug use, the public will react in far different ways and very, very unpleasant ways. But the

01:50:09.400 --> 01:50:14.380
point I would really like to make here is everyone has talked about this public health

01:50:14.380 --> 01:50:19.110
department and that public health department and this hospital and that hospital and how

01:50:19.110 --> 01:50:24.940
we're going to approach the disease. And what is not being said here is that we have no

01:50:24.940 --> 01:50:30.000
federal leadership at the level of the White House. We have no government.

01:50:30.000 --> 01:50:35.340
coming down that are going to be universal I don't mean out of CDC and how

01:50:35.340 --> 01:50:40.960
we should take care of people who are infected in hospitals we have no policy

01:50:40.960 --> 01:50:46.280
that says what will every single health department in the United States be doing

01:50:46.280 --> 01:50:51.900
what will every single school be doing to protect the children we're still

01:50:51.900 --> 01:50:56.940
talking about this disease as if it were a new form of measles or something we

01:50:56.940 --> 01:51:00.000
have a lethal disease we don't know how

01:51:00.000 --> 01:51:04.400
How many of the two million people who are infected are really going to convert?

01:51:04.400 --> 01:51:07.620
This disease is going to run 20 years before we'll know that.

01:51:07.620 --> 01:51:10.350
Ms. McLaughlin, let me go to San Francisco.

01:51:10.350 --> 01:51:11.520
Mr. Reynolds?

01:51:11.520 --> 01:51:12.590
Mr. Reynolds?

01:51:12.590 --> 01:51:13.470
Yes.

01:51:13.470 --> 01:51:14.520
Mr. Reynolds.

01:51:14.520 --> 01:51:15.440
Yes.

01:51:15.440 --> 01:51:16.440
We're talking education.

01:51:16.440 --> 01:51:18.000
Yes.

01:51:18.000 --> 01:51:24.760
We're talking about whether it's possible through education to make serious progress

01:51:24.760 --> 01:51:26.520
with AIDS.

01:51:26.520 --> 01:51:27.960
Do you think it is?

01:51:27.960 --> 01:51:29.540
I think it's very possible.

01:51:30.000 --> 01:51:35.420
many of us that have been working in the AIDS community have been able to touch

01:51:35.420 --> 01:51:40.440
people, to help them look at their fears, to help them gain new understanding and

01:51:40.440 --> 01:51:45.140
information that they have then been able to use to help their friends and

01:51:45.140 --> 01:51:50.520
family members. It's been a ripple effect that I've seen. Thank you Mr. Reynolds.

01:51:50.520 --> 01:51:56.880
Dr. Silverman, we're coming towards the end of our time with this issue.

01:52:00.000 --> 01:52:05.000
what what is the challenge that AIDS presents us and as you see it at this

01:52:05.000 --> 01:52:10.300
point what what what is it going to take for us to get through we're being faced

01:52:10.300 --> 01:52:18.670
with a lethal disease and all of society is is on trial I believe I sincerely

01:52:18.670 --> 01:52:24.380
believe that how society deals with this is going to say a great deal about us as

01:52:24.380 --> 01:52:30.000
individuals we have a indiscriminate virus as was described by dr.

01:52:30.000 --> 01:52:36.310
that doesn't know sexual preference, doesn't know economic, doesn't know color, doesn't

01:52:36.310 --> 01:52:38.210
know ethnicity, none of that.

01:52:38.210 --> 01:52:42.580
If the setting is correct, it can happen.

01:52:42.580 --> 01:52:47.150
We have to get away from the moralistic issues surrounding this.

01:52:47.150 --> 01:52:51.070
We have to have, as Ms. McLaughlin says, leadership from government.

01:52:51.070 --> 01:52:54.790
We can't have a president who says this is the number one health problem and then cuts

01:52:54.790 --> 01:52:59.950
$51 million out of research, prevention, education, community services.

01:53:00.000 --> 01:53:02.560
There is no federal money in community services.

01:53:02.560 --> 01:53:05.700
There's almost no federal money in education.

01:53:05.700 --> 01:53:09.230
We have a disease for which there is no cure and no vaccine.

01:53:09.230 --> 01:53:12.510
The only defense we have is education.

01:53:12.510 --> 01:53:13.990
If we can educate everybody,

01:53:13.990 --> 01:53:15.830
if they will follow what we say,

01:53:15.830 --> 01:53:18.220
we can stop the spread tomorrow.

01:53:18.220 --> 01:53:21.480
- Dr. Silverman, one of the things

01:53:21.480 --> 01:53:23.900
that contributes to the problem, in a sense,

01:53:23.900 --> 01:53:26.740
is the sexual revolution that's taken place in this country

01:53:26.740 --> 01:53:29.640
in the last, say, 30 years.

01:53:31.080 --> 01:53:37.610
It sounds to me, from what you're suggesting, that we have yet another sexual revolution

01:53:37.610 --> 01:53:40.350
in front of us, or maybe a continuation of the one we're on.

01:53:40.350 --> 01:53:42.030
Revolution goes around.

01:53:42.030 --> 01:53:43.180
Revolution goes around.

01:53:43.180 --> 01:53:45.520
And I believe that we are seeing changes.

01:53:45.520 --> 01:53:50.320
One thing that I, Charlie, that I want to stress, I want to stress one thing that keeps

01:53:50.320 --> 01:53:52.670
getting lost, gets glossed over.

01:53:52.670 --> 01:53:58.140
And what was said about New York, San Francisco, and all over, the change of behavior has been

01:53:58.140 --> 01:54:00.000
absolutely phenomenal.

01:54:00.000 --> 01:54:04.540
miraculous. Take 100 people who are overweight, get them to lose weight and keep it off. If you do

01:54:04.540 --> 01:54:10.790
5%, you feel you've been successful. We're talking in terms of 90%. That's incredible change of

01:54:10.790 --> 01:54:15.310
behavior. That's in the gay community. That's in the gay community. And now we're talking also,

01:54:15.710 --> 01:54:20.800
as we extend it, to changes of behavior in the heterosexual community as well. That's correct.

01:54:20.840 --> 01:54:26.840
And there's no reason to believe that heterosexuals will not respond if given the unvarnished truth

01:54:27.760 --> 01:54:30.000
moralism, without bigotry,

01:54:30.000 --> 01:54:36.040
with compassion and sensitivity like we should be giving to the people who are now with AIDS,

01:54:36.360 --> 01:54:41.000
those who could get AIDS. We don't have to talk about, you were saying, should the school do it?

01:54:41.060 --> 01:54:45.210
No, you should do it. But if you don't do it, I don't want your kids to be victims.

01:54:46.680 --> 01:54:51.010
Mr. Lopez, 15 seconds. Last word from you.

01:54:51.010 --> 01:55:00.000
I may eventually die as a result of this disease, but I would consider myself

01:55:00.000 --> 01:55:05.340
death an act of murder for the lack of governmental funding, and I would consider it murder by

01:55:05.340 --> 01:55:07.630
my own government.

01:55:07.630 --> 01:55:09.760
Thank you very much, Mr. Lopez.

01:55:09.760 --> 01:55:15.770
Well the challenge, at least as I see it here, is one of looking at the reality and taking

01:55:15.770 --> 01:55:20.260
off the blinders that seem to come with ignorance and fear.

01:55:20.260 --> 01:55:24.330
Judy, to you.

01:55:24.330 --> 01:55:25.330
Thank you, Charles.

01:55:25.330 --> 01:55:30.000
Tonight we brought you a program that we hope has raised legitimate and important questions

01:55:30.000 --> 01:55:31.980
about our ability to deal with

01:55:31.980 --> 01:55:33.990
this epidemic. Like some

01:55:33.990 --> 01:55:35.970
medieval plague, it has brought out

01:55:35.970 --> 01:55:37.930
our worst fears and prejudices.

01:55:38.290 --> 01:55:40.080
But it is also a test

01:55:40.080 --> 01:55:42.440
of our humanity and our society.

01:55:42.710 --> 01:55:44.480
Because in protecting the rights

01:55:44.480 --> 01:55:45.920
of any one individual,

01:55:46.270 --> 01:55:48.040
we protect all of us.

01:55:48.690 --> 01:55:50.610
For Frontline, I'm Judy Woodruff.

01:55:50.810 --> 01:55:51.270
Good night.

01:55:51.870 --> 01:55:53.770
I'm Howard Brody. I'm

01:55:53.770 --> 01:55:56.610
a specialist in infectious diseases.

01:55:57.160 --> 01:55:58.520
By the time someone's

01:55:58.520 --> 01:56:00.000
got intensively

01:56:00.000 --> 01:56:07.620
ill we've shot our wad as doctors no matter what we do we're gonna lose you

01:56:07.620 --> 01:56:13.020
know it's it's a flashback to the 19th century that's what medicine was there

01:56:13.020 --> 01:56:19.570
to cure never to diagnose rarely to comfort always was the role of the

01:56:19.570 --> 01:56:24.000
physician and that's what we're doing here we're doing 19th century medicine

01:56:24.000 --> 01:56:30.000
okay the virus has taken the entire 20th century medical lady and his fibrinogen was

01:56:30.000 --> 01:56:36.100
166 where lower limb abnormal is 170? That's a good question.

01:56:36.100 --> 01:56:39.640
This is Donald Abrams and I'm the assistant director of the AIDS clinic at San Francisco

01:56:39.640 --> 01:56:47.510
General Hospital. I have probably been directly involved in seeing maybe 2,000 people with

01:56:47.510 --> 01:56:54.620
AIDS and related conditions over the past four years. I've been busy. I spoke to my grandmother

01:56:54.620 --> 01:57:00.000
recently who was 84 years old and she was sort of telling me about her friends who were becoming

01:57:00.000 --> 01:57:04.460
demented and about her friends who were dying, and I said to my grandmother, I said, you

01:57:04.460 --> 01:57:10.840
know, I'm 34 and you're 84, and I think I've had as many friends become demented and die

01:57:10.840 --> 01:57:12.580
as you have, and that's not really fair.

01:57:12.580 --> 01:57:18.430
I mean, it gets to be devastating.

01:57:18.430 --> 01:57:24.920
My name is Gayling Gee, I'm the head nurse of the outpatient Ward 86 AIDS clinic.

01:57:24.920 --> 01:57:29.510
I think one of the strengths of our clinic is that it is okay to cry in clinic.

01:57:30.060 --> 01:57:32.960
But I think two weeks ago, I was in a staff meeting,

01:57:32.960 --> 01:57:34.560
and I said, this is it.

01:57:34.560 --> 01:57:35.440
This is enough.

01:57:35.440 --> 01:57:36.400
I know it's tough.

01:57:36.400 --> 01:57:38.400
It has been a terrible month.

01:57:38.400 --> 01:57:42.820
We had about 27, 30 deaths, and we wrote all the names

01:57:42.820 --> 01:57:43.800
on the board.

01:57:43.800 --> 01:57:46.180
But I am not going to let you sit here and cry all the time.

01:57:46.180 --> 01:57:48.700
You have work to do, and you've got to keep going.

01:57:48.700 --> 01:57:51.380
Because there are still people out there who are counting on you.

01:57:51.380 --> 01:57:53.460
And Brokowski might give us our answer.

01:57:53.460 --> 01:57:55.930
Might be a better way to go.

01:57:55.930 --> 01:57:56.430
Yeah.

01:57:56.430 --> 01:57:57.910
If they're going to do it anyway.

01:57:57.910 --> 01:57:58.560
Yeah.

01:57:58.560 --> 01:58:00.000
My name is Paul Scherer.

01:58:00.060 --> 01:58:05.640
And I'm a counselor with the Shanti Project on 5B, the AIDS ward, at General Hospital.

01:58:05.860 --> 01:58:09.760
I think there are a lot of issues with AIDS that are analogous to warfare.

01:58:10.320 --> 01:58:13.740
We have certainly the combat fatigue in terms of the caregivers.

01:58:14.920 --> 01:58:19.620
Vast numbers of young men dying is something that's endemic in war, but not in peacetime.

01:58:19.620 --> 01:58:24.540
So we have parents burying their sons, and that's not the way it's supposed to be.

